{"abstract":[{"text":"Identity-independent presentation-attack-detection verdict for one","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"frame, fused from the PAD signals only (the liveness CNN + TrueDepth)."}],"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"platforms":["iOS","iPadOS","Mac Catalyst"],"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"enum","kind":"keyword"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"PADVerdict"}]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Overview","anchor":"overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"FaceEvaluationResult.trusted"},{"text":" fuses PAD ","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"and"}]},{"text":" face-recognition identity,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"so a lab measuring ISO\/IEC 30107-3 spoof resistance (APCER\/BPCER \/","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"IAPMR) cannot read pure PAD off it — an unenrolled genuine face reads"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"trusted == false"},{"type":"text","text":" purely because of the identity gate. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"padVerdict"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"isolates the PAD decision so the spoof metric is read off one field,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"independent of enrolment:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.youreyeonly.yeofr.YEOFR\/documentation\/YEOFR\/PADVerdict\/genuine"},{"text":" — the PAD signals admit a live\/3D presentation.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.youreyeonly.yeofr.YEOFR\/documentation\/YEOFR\/PADVerdict\/spoof","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" — the PAD signals reject the presentation (flat depth and\/or","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"a CNN spoof ver